        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Pass the Trash',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Pass the Trash is a stud poker variant in which each player receives seven cards, posts antes, and after a betting round passes three unwanted cards to the next active player to the left. After a second betting round players discard two cards, order the remaining five face down, then reveal them one at a time with betting between each reveal. The highest five-card hand at showdown wins the pot.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: USA\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 to 7 players. Best with 4. No partnerships.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck. One deck. No jokers.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card deck, poker chips for antes and betting.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'After antes are placed, seven cards are dealt face down to each player. Dealing is clockwise.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'High-Low: Before showdown everyone declares high, low, or both (e.g. chips in fist); high and low winners split the pot.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Three-phase pass: First phase: three cards passed left. Second: two cards passed two places left. Third: one card passed three places left. Betting round after each phase.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Pot split with next right: Pot is split between the high hand and the next active player to the right (the one who received your passed cards).',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
